exports[`CLI help interface for 'config delete journeys' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo config delete journeys [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Experimental] Delete one journey by id, or delete all journeys and clean up
orphaned nodes in the selected realms. A journey that other objects still name
is not deleted without --force.

Arguments:
  host                   AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am. To
                         use a connection profile, just specify a unique
                         substring or alias.
  realm                  Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or
                         'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default: "alpha"
                         for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username               Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                         appropriate rights to manage authentication
                         journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                         matches the username already stored in the connection
                         profile for the target host, frodo uses that profile's
                         stored password instead of requiring it on the command
                         line.
  password               Password.

Options:
  --allow-failures       Report operations that fail, but still exit with code
                         0. Without this option the command runs every
                         operation, prints a summary of what failed and exits
                         with code 1.
  -d, --dry-run          Show what would be deleted or changed without deleting
                         or changing anything.
  --force                Delete the journey with -i although other objects still
                         name it. First the journey is cleared in the OAuth2
                         clients, SAML providers and AI agents that name it, and
                         removed from the themes that link it. Every other
                         object that names it is left alone, it names a journey
                         that does not exist afterwards. What was cleared and
                         what was left is printed. Only with -i.
  -i, --journey-id <id>  Id (name) of the journey to delete. Requires a realm
                         argument. If it is left out, all journeys are deleted.
                         (alias: -n, --name)
  --keep-links           With --force: leave the links of the themes to the
                         journey as they are. Only with -i and --force.
  -y, --yes              Do not ask for confirmation before deleting all
                         journeys, or before deleting a journey with --force.
                         Required without a terminal.
  -h, --help             Help
  -hh, --help-more       Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all       Help with all options, environment variables, and usage
                         examples.
"
`;
